    ],
    "biography": "Dr. Magna Soelma Beserra de Moura is a researcher at Embrapa Tropical Agroindustry in Brazil, specializing in agrometeorology. She holds a Ph.D. in Natural Resources from the Federal University of Campina Grande. Her research focuses on evapotranspiration, energy balance, phenology, remote sensing and CO2 fluxes in agricultural and natural ecosystems, particularly the Brazilian Caatinga biome. Her work has established the Caatinga as a highly efficient carbon sink, contributing significantly to understanding dry tropical forest dynamics.",
    "startYear": 2013,
    "email": "magna.moura@embrapa.br",
